### TITLE ###
LongLinesWrapWithAHangingIndent
### DESCRIPTION ###
A prompt truncates; an editor cannot, because the text is what you are working
on. The buffer soft-wraps itself so each frame line is still exactly one visual
row, which is what the inline renderer's redraw accounting depends on. Note no
row reaches the full width: a row filled to the width triggers the terminal's
own wrap and desyncs that accounting.
### PROMPT ###
>
### WIDTH ###
12
### KEYS ###
"abcdefghijklmnopq"
enter
### VALUE ###
abcdefghijklmnopq
### OUTCOME ###
submitted
